    "article_summary": "This article describes a chemoenzymatic cascade that integrates nitrilase (NIT) enzymes with photoredox catalysis to convert organic nitriles into fluorinated, trifluoromethylated, and pentafluoroethylated products. The process involves the enzymatic hydrolysis of nitriles to carboxylic acids in aqueous buffer, followed by in situ photoredox-catalyzed decarboxylative functionalization using reagents like Selectfluor or Togni's reagent.",
